# TUI-DESIGN-4 §7.3 item 6 / §10 S6: `render:live`. The live region (`layout.live`) is the streaming slot, and it
# is allocated only while the run has live text to show — the decisions panel takes those rows when it is open,
# which is why this scenario does NOT open the panel (`fault-run.steps` does, for `pane` and `overlay`).
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
sleep 0.5
send start the fault run
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[run\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* started [·-] 
sleep 3
send \x03
expect Follow-up, question|Say hi
sleep 0.4
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
